# Bbox axis order

**Single authority:** `src/satmap_dataset/geo/bbox.py`

## Project convention (config, manifests, CLI `--bbox`, render target grid)

`xmin,ymin,xmax,ymax` in logical (x,y) order. For EPSG:2180: **(easting, northing)**.

Do not add implicit SRS-keyed swaps in cli.py or render.py.

## WFS / GUGiK skorowidz query

OGC WFS `BBOX` uses CRS authority axis order. EPSG:2180 authority order is (northing, easting).

Use `geo.bbox.wfs_query_bbox_str(project_bbox, srs)` at every WFS query boundary.
Use `geo.bbox.wfs_query_axes_swapped(srs)` for manifest `wfs_bbox_axes_swapped`.

## Deprecated

`experimental_wfs_swap_bbox_axes` is ignored for EPSG:2180 (auto-swap). Do not reintroduce compensating swap/unswap pairs.

## Separate concern: TIFF georef

Downloaded tile tie points may be axis-swapped vs project order. Render infers `source_axis_mode` (`normal`/`swapped`) from georef — not bbox strings. Do not conflate with `geo.bbox`.

## Feature bbox normalization

`geoportal/wfs_client.py` normalizes per-feature bboxes to project order via overlap against the WFS query bbox. Stored `tile_bboxes_by_year` must be project-order.
